      "content": "The consensus among urban planners and economists is that high-density housing is the only viable solution to the current housing crisis, as it increases supply and lowers costs for everyone.\nRelying on single-family zoning to \"protect community\" is a deliberate political strategy by wealthy developers to artificially inflate prices and exclude working-class families.\nCities that embrace mixed-use, high-density development create vibrant, walkable neighborhoods that foster true community connection rather than the isolation of sprawling suburbs.\nTherefore, the debate isn't really about community values but about whether we want affordable housing or a system rigged for the rich.",
